  "notes": "Composed of {注|ちゅう} (note, attention) + {記|き} (write, record). Used for supplementary information added to documents, maps, charts, and other written materials.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {注記|ちゅうき}を{加|くわ}える — to add notes/annotations\n- {注記|ちゅうき}を{付|つ}ける — to attach annotations\n- {注記|ちゅうき}を{参照|さんしょう}する — to refer to the notes\n- {注記|ちゅうき}{事項|じこう} — annotated items; noted matters\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {注釈|ちゅうしゃく} — commentary, footnote (more detailed explanation, often scholarly)\n- {備考|びこう} — remarks, notes (used in tables and forms)\n- メモ — memo, note (informal; personal notes)\n- {脚注|きゃくちゅう} — footnote (specifically at the bottom of a page)\n- {補足|ほそく} — supplement, additional information",
